Physicians should provide fluoride varnish **from tooth eruption until the beneficiary reaches 3½ years of age**. The related oral screening service is also limited to beneficiaries **under 3½ years of age**. [Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment) (effective 2019-12-04), §§ 7.2, 5.3.1, 5.3.2.

## Oral screening requirements

The policy requires the oral screening package to include:

- **Early caries screening** and detection of notable findings in the oral cavity, including obvious hard- and soft-tissue pathology, using **a dental mirror and directed light**;
- **Counseling and educational materials** on good oral hygiene practices and nutrition for children;
- **Prescribing a fluoride supplement, if indicated**; and
- **Application of fluoride varnish** to all erupted primary teeth beginning at tooth eruption until age 3½. [Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), § 7.2.

## Billing/coverage limits tied to the screening

The policy’s billing codes add these limits:

- **D0145**: oral evaluation for a patient under 3 years of age and counseling with the primary caregiver, but policy states it is **limited to beneficiaries under 3½ years of age**;
- **D1206**: topical fluoride varnish treatment, also **limited to beneficiaries under 3½ years of age**;
- Both must be billed **together**;
- Allowed **once every 60 calendar days**; and
- Limited to **six times before the beneficiary reaches 3½ years of age**. [Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), §§ 5.3.1, 5.3.2.

## Documentation required

The beneficiary’s health record must document:

- the **oral evaluation** and any notable findings;
- **preventive oral health and dietary counseling** with the primary caregiver;
- **application of fluoride varnish**; and
- **referral to a dentist, if appropriate**. [Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), § 7.2.

